Blues beat the slumping Pittsburgh Penguins 5-2 on Thursday night.","story":"PITTSBURGH -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080171/jimmy-snuggerud\">Jimmy Snuggerud</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697397/dylan-holloway\">Dylan Holloway</a> each scored twice as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/stl/st-louis-blues\">St. Louis Blues</a> beat the slumping <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/pit/pittsburgh-penguins\">Pittsburgh Penguins</a> 5-2 on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697408/justin-barron\">Justin Barron</a> also had a goal and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233637/robert-thomas\">Robert Thomas</a> finished with three assists for the Blues, who have won four of five. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587909/joel-hofer\">Joel Hofer</a> made 31 saves.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2562629/rickard-rakell\">Rickard Rakell</a> scored twice for the Penguins, who have lost seven of nine and are mired near the bottom of the Eastern Conference.\n\n\r\n              Snuggerud ended the second period with a goal and added his team-leading 12th in the third. St. Louis scored three times and outshot the Penguins 22-10 in the second period to take command. \n\n\r\n              The Blues are 9-0 when leading through two periods. They had five goals in their previous four games before breaking out for 13 combined in wins against Anaheim and Pittsburgh.\n\n\r\n              Holloway has a three-game point streak. Thomas, who has six points in his last two games, upped his career total to 344 assists — moving past <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4013/alex-pietrangelo\">Alex Pietrangelo</a> for third in franchise history.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697409/jake-neighbours\">Jake Neighbours</a> added two assists for St. Louis.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3124/evgeni-malkin\">Evgeni Malkin</a> had an assist for Pittsburgh and is tied with Bryan Trottier for 19th place in NHL history with 1,425 points. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3539/kris-letang\">Kris Letang</a> added an assist and is tied with Tampa Bay's <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5157/victor-hedman\">Victor Hedman</a> for the eighth-most points by a defenseman with one franchise.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4576894/arturs-silovs\">Arturs Silovs</a> stopped 28 shots for the Penguins, who had won six straight against St. Louis at home.\n\n\r\n              Rakell had the lone first-period goal, tipping in a shot from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3025524/trevor-van-riemsdyk\">Trevor van Riemsdyk</a>, who hadn’t played since Oct. 10 because of a lower-body injury.\n\n\r\n              Goals by Barron, Holloway and Snuggerud gave the Blues a 3-1 lead through two periods.\n\n\r\n              Barron and Holloway scored shortly after St. Louis power plays expired, and Snuggerud put a rebound behind Silovs on an odd-man rush.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Blues: Host the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nj/new-jersey-devils\">New Jersey Devils</a> on Saturday and play eight of their next nine games at home.\n\n\r\n              Penguins: Visit the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nsh/nashville-predators\">Nashville Predators</a> on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-20T03:17:34Z"}}